function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    var page := dval({source_page: ""})
    page["source_page"] = "capy-06-strings-and-markup"
    page["kind"] = "guide"
    page["slug"] = "strings-and-markup"
    page["route"] = "/doc/guide/strings-and-markup/"
    page["title"] = "6. Strings and HTML"
    page["content"] = "Use strings for text and markup expressions for HTML. Markup escapes ordinary strings before they enter the response.\n\n## Escape dynamic text\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"<Ada>\"\n    print(<><p>Hello, <?= name ?></p></>, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n<p>Hello, &lt;Ada&gt;</p>\n\n```\n\n`<?= name ?>` selects an encoding from its location. HTML text and quoted attributes escape `&`, `<`, `>`, quotes, and apostrophes.\n\nInside a `script` element, a string becomes one self-contained JavaScript literal. The encoder protects the closing tag and JavaScript line separators. Inside a `style` element, a string becomes one self-contained CSS literal. Integer and Boolean values remain scalar values. `f64` interpolation is not supported in these elements.\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := string(request.query.name, \"guest\")\n    print(<>\n        <script>const name = <?= name ?>;</script>\n        <style>.name::before { content: <?= name ?>; }</style>\n    </>)\n}\n\n```\n\n\nScript and style interpolation must start at a value boundary. Static source after it can apply an operator or a CSS unit. Do not put interpolation inside an existing string, template literal, or comment. Attribute values must use quotes. Tag and attribute names cannot contain interpolation.\n\nURL, event-handler, and inline-style attributes use HTML attribute escaping. Validate these values for their application context before interpolation.\n\n## String literals\n\nString literals use double quotes:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var message := \"Hello\"\n    var line := \"first\\nsecond\"\n    print(message, \" \", line, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThe supported escapes include `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\\"`, and `\\\\`. String positions and lengths count bytes, not Unicode characters.\n"
    page["content"] = string(page["content"], "") + "\nUse `+` to join strings:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"Ada\"\n    var greeting := \"Hello, \" + name\n    print(greeting, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nUse a constructor to convert a scalar when a function does not already accept `as string`:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var label := \"Count: \" + string(3)\n    print(label, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\n## Markup expressions\n\nA markup expression starts with `<>` and ends with `</>`:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var title := \"Report\"\n    print(<>\n        <h1><?= title ?></h1>\n        <p>Ready</p>\n    </>)\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThe expression has type `markup`. It is a value. It does not write to the response by itself. Use `print(markup_value)` to output it. You can also return `markup` from an ordinary function or insert it into other markup.\n\n```capy\nfunction badge(label : string) markup {\n    -> <><strong><?= label ?></strong></>\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(badge(\"Ready\"))\n}\n\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n<strong>Ready</strong>\n\n```\n\n\n## Interpolation rule\n\n`<?= value ?>` escapes output at the interpolation site. `<?: value ?>` emits output without escaping. It works only in HTML text.\n\nThe interpolation form selects escaping. The value type does not.\n\n## Common string operations\n\nUse `length`, `substr`, `find`, `contains`, `replace`, `lower`, `upper`, `split`, and `join` for ordinary text work. Use `html_escape` when an API needs escaped text instead of a `markup` value.\n\nStrings use automatic reference counting. Assignment and function calls preserve their lifetime. Most programs do not need to call `clone`.\n"
    page["label"] = "6. Strings and HTML"
    page["capy_sig_lines"] = dval([])
    page["param_lines"] = dval([])
    page["notes"] = dval([])
    page["warnings"] = dval([])
    page["see"] = dval([{label: "string", href: "/doc/type/string/"}, {label: "html_escape", href: "/doc/api/html-escape/"}, {label: "5. Functions", href: "/doc/guide/functions-and-closures/"}, {label: "9. Handling a web request", href: "/doc/guide/web-handlers-and-requests/"}, {label: "string", href: "/doc/api/string/"}, {label: "length", href: "/doc/api/length/"}, {label: "clone", href: "/doc/api/clone/"}])
    page["examples"] = dval([])
    page["guide_examples"] = dval([{entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"<Ada>\"\n    print(<><p>Hello, <?= name ?></p></>, \"\\n\")\n}\n", output: "<p>Hello, &lt;Ada&gt;</p>\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := string(request.query.name, \"guest\")\n    print(<>\n        <script>const name = <?= name ?>;</script>\n        <style>.name::before { content: <?= name ?>; }</style>\n    </>)\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var message := \"Hello\"\n    var line := \"first\\nsecond\"\n    print(message, \" \", line, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"Ada\"\n    var greeting := \"Hello, \" + name\n    print(greeting, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var label := \"Count: \" + string(3)\n    print(label, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var title := \"Report\"\n    print(<>\n        <h1><?= title ?></h1>\n        <p>Ready</p>\n    </>)\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function badge(label : string) markup {\n    -> <><strong><?= label ?></strong></>\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(badge(\"Ready\"))\n}\n", output: "<strong>Ready</strong>\n"}])
    component_render("/doc/components/doc_page.capy", page)
}
